<p class="lede">Telling a team that low contrast is a problem changes very little. Handing them a booking reference they cannot read, and asking them to say it out loud, changes quite a lot.</p>

<p>These are the exercises I use in <strong>accessibility discovery sessions</strong>: an hour or so with a product team, where everyone does the task rather than watches a slide about it. Each one has a scenario, a task, a deliberately broken interface, and a switch to the version that works. They run in a browser, they need no software and no setup, and they work just as well on a call as in a room.</p>

<p>Take what is useful. Run them in any order, or pick the two that match the thing your team is arguing about this week.</p>

